{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Try to think about $f$ as a transformation of the parent function $y=|x|$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"These are the transformations performed on $y=|x|$ to get $f(x)=\\purpleD{-2}|x-\\greenD{(-4)}|+\\blueD{0}$:\n\n1. Shift $\\greenD{-4}$ units horizontally (i.e. $4$ units to the left).\n2. Stretch by a factor of $\\purpleD{-2}$.\n\nThis tells us that the vertex of the graph is at $(\\greenD{-4},\\blueD{0})$.\n\nIt also tells us that if we move $1$ unit to the right from the vertex, we should go $\\purpleD{2}$ units down.\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, this is the graph of $f$:\n\n[[☃ grapher 5]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"grapher 5":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"availableTypes":["absolute_value"],"correct":{"coords":[[-4,0],[-3,-2]],"type":"absolute_value"},"graph":{"backgroundImage":{"url":null},"editableSettings":["graph","snap","image"],"gridStep":[1,1],"labels":["x","y"],"markings":"graph","range":[[-8,8],[-8,8]],"rulerLabel":"","rulerTicks":10,"showProtractor":false,"showRuler":false,"showTooltips":false,"snapStep":[1,1],"step":[1,1],"valid":true}},"static":true,"type":"grapher","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Graph $f(x)=-2|x +4|$.**\n\n[[☃ grapher 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"grapher 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"availableTypes":["absolute_value"],"correct":{"coords":[[-4,0],[-3,-2]],"type":"absolute_value"},"graph":{"backgroundImage":{"url":null},"editableSettings":["graph","snap","image"],"gridStep":[1,1],"labels":["x","y"],"markings":"graph","range":[[-8,8],[-8,8]],"rulerLabel":"","rulerTicks":10,"showProtractor":false,"showRuler":false,"showTooltips":false,"snapStep":[1,1],"step":[1,1],"valid":true}},"static":false,"type":"grapher","version":